https://solodit.cyfrin.io/issues/denial-.audit_content:
Vaults Without a Knock-In Event
Vaults without a knock-in event may be permanently frozen by calling
fcnCheckBarriers
before settlement. This happens because
fcnCheckTradeExpiry
attempts to add
type(uint16).max
to the number of price observations, reverting if the prior value is larger than zero.
contracts/cega-strategies/fcn/lib/FCNVaultLogic.sol
----new code block----
function checkBarriers(
 /* ... */
) internal returns (bool isKnockedIn, uint16 observationsCount) {
 /* ... */
 if (isKnockedIn) {
        fcnVault.observationsDone = type(uint16).max;
        fcnVault.isKnockedIn = true;
    } else {
        fcnVault.observationsDone += maxObservations;
    }
}
function checkTradeExpiry(
 /* ... */
) internal {
 /* ... */
    (bool isKnockedIn, ) = checkBarriers(
        cgs,
        addressManager,
        vaultAddress,
 type(uint16).max
    );
 /* ... */
}
----end of code block ----
Proof of Concept
The vault may be permanently frozen via the following sequence:
A malicious user calls
fcnCheckBarriers
with a max observation count of one. This results in
observationsDone
to become one.
All Knock-In (KI) barriers are not reached, resulting in a non-KI vault.
The market maker calls
checkTradeExpiry
for settlement, but encounters a revert due to an integer overflow. Because the vault cannot be settled, any further state transitions may not occur.
