Impact
Short-Term Impact:
Arithmetic Underflow:
Vote updates involving increased voting power trigger an underflow error, causing the vote transaction to revert.
Vote Failure:
Users cannot update their vote if their voting power increases, leading to a denial of service on vote changes.
Long-Term Impact:
Reward Distribution Distortion:
Gauge weights directly affect reward allocations; incorrect weights can lead to unfair distribution.
Governance Instability:
The gauge system is used for governance; persistent inaccuracies can undermine trust and fairness.
User Frustration and Abuse:
Users may be prevented from properly casting or updating votes, opening the door for potential manipulative or abusive behaviors.
